IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-periods`
IMPORT `sg-definitions`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition: ss 76H, 76I, 76J and 76K -- treasury shares: holding them, the 10% ceiling, what the company may not do with them,
-- and how the company may dispose of or cancel them.
-- Layer 1 (the law, objectively). Lines 9051-9242 of inputs/CoA1967.txt (a rendering, not the official text).
-- Reading a result: JUST TRUE is yes, JUST FALSE is the text saying no in its own words, NOTHING is "the text does not say".
-- Tags {F-..} point at the fork register and {MR-a}, {MR-b} at the marginal readings for a lawyer (NOTES.md).

§ `Section 76H: treasury shares`

-- The keel's s 4(1) "treasury share" asks whether the share "was (or is treated as having been) purchased by a company in circumstances in which section 76H applies".
-- This function answers that fact for the shares s 76H(1) names.
-- src:9053 | 76H.—(1) Where ordinary shares or stocks are purchased or
-- src:9054 | otherwise acquired by a company in accordance with sections 76B
-- src:9055 | to 76G, the company may —
-- src:9057 | (a) hold the shares or stocks (or any of them); or
-- src:9059 | (b) deal with any of them, at any time, in accordance with
-- src:9060 | section 76K.
@ref s 76H(1) (src:9053-9060)
GIVEN `the shares or stocks are ordinary shares or stocks` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the shares or stocks are purchased or otherwise acquired by the company in accordance with sections 76B to 76G` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76H(1) section 76H applies to the shares or stocks` MEANS
    IF    `the shares or stocks are ordinary shares or stocks`
      AND `the shares or stocks are purchased or otherwise acquired by the company in accordance with sections 76B to 76G`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where ordinary shares or stocks are purchased or otherwise acquired by a company in accordance with sections 76B to 76G"; preference shares and shares acquired some other way are outside it {F-H1} {MR-b}

-- src:9053 | 76H.—(1) Where ordinary shares or stocks are purchased or
-- src:9054 | otherwise acquired by a company in accordance with sections 76B
-- src:9055 | to 76G, the company may —
-- src:9057 | (a) hold the shares or stocks (or any of them); or
@ref s 76H(1)(a) (src:9053-9057)
GIVEN `section 76H applies to the shares or stocks` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76H(1)(a) the company may hold the shares or stocks` MEANS
    IF `section 76H applies to the shares or stocks`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a grant ("the company may — (a) hold the shares or stocks (or any of them)") whose "Where" gate failed; the grant rule of 2026-11-12, limit 1 (and, for a "where" gate, limit 3, fork F-H2) {F-H2} {MR-b}

-- src:9053 | 76H.—(1) Where ordinary shares or stocks are purchased or
-- src:9054 | otherwise acquired by a company in accordance with sections 76B
-- src:9059 | (b) deal with any of them, at any time, in accordance with
-- src:9060 | section 76K.
@ref s 76H(1)(b) (src:9053-9060)
GIVEN `section 76H applies to the shares or stocks` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76H(1)(b) the company may deal with the shares or stocks, at any time, in accordance with section 76K` MEANS
    IF `section 76H applies to the shares or stocks`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a grant ("the company may — ... or (b) deal with any of them, at any time, in accordance with section 76K") whose "Where" gate failed; the grant rule of 2026-11-12, limit 1 (and, for a "where" gate, limit 3, fork F-H2) {F-H2} {MR-b}

-- src:9062 | (2) Where ordinary shares or stocks are held under
-- src:9063 | subsection (1)(a) then, for the purposes of section 190 (Register
-- src:9064 | and index of members) and section 196A (Electronic register of
-- src:9065 | members), the company must be entered in the register as the member
-- src:9066 | holding those shares or stocks.
@ref s 76H(2) (src:9062-9066)
GIVEN `the ordinary shares or stocks are held by the company under section 76H(1)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76H(2) the company is entered in the register as the member holding the shares or stocks` MEANS
    IF `the ordinary shares or stocks are held by the company under section 76H(1)(a)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where ordinary shares or stocks are held under subsection (1)(a) then, for the purposes of section 190 ... and section 196A ..., the company must be entered in the register as the member holding those shares or stocks"; other shares are outside it {MR-b}

§ `Section 76I: treasury shares, maximum holdings`

-- (1) and (2): the 10% ceiling is a bar. TRUE: the number held is more than 10% of the total at that time. "the total number of shares of the company at that time" is counted with the treasury shares in it (fork F-I1).
-- src:9072 | 76I.—(1) Where a company has shares of only one class, the
-- src:9073 | aggregate number of shares held as treasury shares must not at any
-- src:9078 | time exceed 10% of the total number of shares of the company at that
-- src:9079 | time.
@ref s 76I(1) (src:9072-9079)
GIVEN `the company has shares of only one class` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the aggregate number of shares held as treasury shares` IS A NUMBER
      `the total number of shares of the company at that time, treasury shares included` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76I(1) the number of shares held as treasury shares exceeds the limit` MEANS
    IF NOT `the company has shares of only one class`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a company has shares of only one class, the aggregate number of shares held as treasury shares must not at any time exceed 10%" -- the "Where" fails, so subsection (1) bars nothing (the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b)); subsection (2) is the rule for a company with several classes {F-I2} {MR-a}
    ELSE (IF (`the aggregate number of shares held as treasury shares` TIMES 100) GREATER THAN (10 TIMES `the total number of shares of the company at that time, treasury shares included`)
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must not at any time exceed 10% of the total number of shares of the company at that time" (a flat negative) {F-I1} {MR-a}

-- src:9081 | (2) Where the share capital of a company is divided into shares of
-- src:9082 | different classes, the aggregate number of the shares of any class held
-- src:9083 | as treasury shares must not at any time exceed 10% of the total
-- src:9084 | number of the shares in that class at that time.
@ref s 76I(2) (src:9081-9084)
GIVEN `the share capital of the company is divided into shares of different classes` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the aggregate number of the shares of the class held as treasury shares` IS A NUMBER
      `the total number of the shares in that class at that time, treasury shares included` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76I(2) the number of shares of the class held as treasury shares exceeds the limit` MEANS
    IF NOT `the share capital of the company is divided into shares of different classes`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the share capital of a company is divided into shares of different classes, the aggregate number of the shares of any class held as treasury shares must not at any time exceed 10%" -- the "Where" fails, so subsection (2) bars nothing (the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b)); subsection (1) is the rule for a company with one class {F-I2} {MR-a}
    ELSE (IF (`the aggregate number of the shares of the class held as treasury shares` TIMES 100) GREATER THAN (10 TIMES `the total number of the shares in that class at that time, treasury shares included`)
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must not at any time exceed 10% of the total number of the shares in that class at that time" (a flat negative) {F-I1} {MR-a}

-- (4): "the excess shares" means such number of the shares, held as treasury shares at the time in question, as resulted in the limit being exceeded.
-- Taken: the number held less the whole shares that 10% of the total allows (a part of a share does not count as allowed; fork F-I3).
-- src:9092 | (4) In subsection (3), “the excess shares” means such number of the
-- src:9093 | shares, held by the company as treasury shares at the time in question,
-- src:9094 | as resulted in the limit being exceeded.
@ref s 76I(4) (src:9092-9094)
GIVEN `the number of the shares held as treasury shares at the time in question` IS A NUMBER
      `the total number of the shares at that time, treasury shares included` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 76I(4) the number of the excess shares` MEANS
    IF `the number of the shares held as treasury shares at the time in question` GREATER THAN (FLOOR ((10 TIMES `the total number of the shares at that time, treasury shares included`) DIVIDED BY 100))
    THEN `the number of the shares held as treasury shares at the time in question` MINUS (FLOOR ((10 TIMES `the total number of the shares at that time, treasury shares included`) DIVIDED BY 100))
    ELSE 0

-- (3): "before the end of the period of 6 months beginning with the day on which that contravention occurs, or such further period as the Registrar may allow".
-- The 6 months begin on the day of the contravention (that day is the first), so they end the day before the same date 6 months on (fork F-P1).
-- Where the month 6 months on has no such date (31 August: February has no 31st), there is no "same date" to step back from, so the 6 months end on the last day of that month (the keel's P4: 31 August plus 6 months is 28 February). Stepping the clamped date back by one day would end the period a day early; the test is whether stepping the clamped date back 6 months returns the day of the contravention.
-- src:9086 | (3) Where subsection (1) or (2) is contravened by a company, the
-- src:9087 | company must dispose of or cancel the excess shares in accordance
-- src:9088 | with section 76K before the end of the period of 6 months beginning
-- src:9089 | with the day on which that contravention occurs, or such further
-- src:9090 | period as the Registrar may allow.
@ref s 76I(3) (src:9086-9090)
GIVEN `the day on which the contravention occurs` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 76I(3) the last day of the 6 months beginning with the day on which the contravention occurs` MEANS
    IF (`period: the latest day for an act a period before` (`period: the last day of a period after` `the day on which the contravention occurs` 6 Months) 6 Months) EQUALS `the day on which the contravention occurs`
    THEN `period: the latest day for an act a period before` (`period: the last day of a period after` `the day on which the contravention occurs` 6 Months) 1 Days
    ELSE `period: the last day of a period after` `the day on which the contravention occurs` 6 Months

-- src:9086 | (3) Where subsection (1) or (2) is contravened by a company, the
-- src:9087 | company must dispose of or cancel the excess shares in accordance
-- src:9088 | with section 76K before the end of the period of 6 months beginning
-- src:9089 | with the day on which that contravention occurs, or such further
-- src:9090 | period as the Registrar may allow.
@ref s 76I(3) (src:9086-9090)
GIVEN `the day on which the contravention occurs` IS A DATE
      `the Registrar has allowed a further period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the last day of the further period the Registrar has allowed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 76I(3) the last day for the company to dispose of or cancel the excess shares` MEANS
    IF `the Registrar has allowed a further period`
    THEN `the last day of the further period the Registrar has allowed`
    ELSE `s 76I(3) the last day of the 6 months beginning with the day on which the contravention occurs` `the day on which the contravention occurs`

-- src:9086 | (3) Where subsection (1) or (2) is contravened by a company, the
-- src:9087 | company must dispose of or cancel the excess shares in accordance
-- src:9088 | with section 76K before the end of the period of 6 months beginning
-- src:9089 | with the day on which that contravention occurs, or such further
-- src:9090 | period as the Registrar may allow.
@ref s 76I(3) (src:9086-9090)
GIVEN `the day on which the contravention occurs` IS A DATE
      `the Registrar has allowed a further period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the last day of the further period the Registrar has allowed` IS A DATE
      `the company has disposed of or cancelled the excess shares in accordance with section 76K` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the excess shares were disposed of or cancelled` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76I(3) the company has disposed of or cancelled the excess shares in time` MEANS
    IF    `the company has disposed of or cancelled the excess shares in accordance with section 76K`
      AND `the day the excess shares were disposed of or cancelled` AT MOST `s 76I(3) the last day for the company to dispose of or cancel the excess shares` `the day on which the contravention occurs` `the Registrar has allowed a further period` `the last day of the further period the Registrar has allowed`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the company must dispose of or cancel the excess shares in accordance with section 76K before the end of the period of 6 months beginning with the day on which that contravention occurs, or such further period as the Registrar may allow" (a duty not met, the provision's own question) {F-I4} {MR-a}

DECLARE `s 76I act` IS ONE OF
    `s 76I(3) dispose of or cancel the excess shares in accordance with section 76K`

-- The clock of the rule runs in days from the day of the contravention (day 0); the caller works out the last day with the functions above and gives the number of days.
-- src:9086 | (3) Where subsection (1) or (2) is contravened by a company, the
-- src:9087 | company must dispose of or cancel the excess shares in accordance
-- src:9088 | with section 76K before the end of the period of 6 months beginning
-- src:9089 | with the day on which that contravention occurs, or such further
-- src:9090 | period as the Registrar may allow.
@ref s 76I(3) (src:9086-9090)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
      `the number of days from the day on which the contravention occurs to the last day for disposal or cancellation` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 76I act`
`s 76I(3) the company must dispose of or cancel the excess shares before the end of the period` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 76I(3) dispose of or cancel the excess shares in accordance with section 76K`
    WITHIN `the number of days from the day on which the contravention occurs to the last day for disposal or cancellation`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the company did not dispose of or cancel the excess shares before the end of the period allowed"

§ `Section 76J: treasury shares, voting and other rights`

-- src:9098 | 76J.—(1) This section applies to shares which are held by a
-- src:9099 | company as treasury shares.
-- src:9101 | (2) The company must not exercise any right in respect of the
-- src:9102 | treasury shares and any purported exercise of such a right is void.
@ref s 76J(2) (src:9098-9102)
GIVEN `the shares are held by the company as treasury shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company purports to exercise a right in respect of the treasury shares` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76J(2) the purported exercise by the company of a right in respect of the treasury shares is void` MEANS
    IF `the shares are held by the company as treasury shares` AND `the company purports to exercise a right in respect of the treasury shares`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This section applies to shares which are held by a company as treasury shares" and speaks of "any purported exercise of such a right"; other shares, and a case with no purported exercise, are outside it {MR-b}

-- src:9098 | 76J.—(1) This section applies to shares which are held by a
-- src:9099 | company as treasury shares.
-- src:9104 | (3) The rights to which subsection (2) applies include any right to
-- src:9105 | attend or vote at meetings (including meetings under section 210) and
-- src:9106 | for the purposes of this Act, the company is to be treated as having no
-- src:9107 | right to vote and the treasury shares are to be treated as having no
-- src:9108 | voting rights.
@ref s 76J(3) (src:9098-9108)
GIVEN `the shares are held by the company as treasury shares` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76J(3) the company has a right to vote on the treasury shares` MEANS
    IF `the shares are held by the company as treasury shares`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the company is to be treated as having no right to vote and the treasury shares are to be treated as having no voting rights" (a flat negative) {MR-a}
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This section applies to shares which are held by a company as treasury shares"; other shares are outside it {MR-b}

-- (4): no dividend may be paid, and no other distribution made, to the company in respect of the treasury shares. A bar: TRUE where the payment is one it forbids.
-- src:9098 | 76J.—(1) This section applies to shares which are held by a
-- src:9099 | company as treasury shares.
-- src:9110 | (4) No dividend may be paid, and no other distribution (whether in
-- src:9111 | cash or otherwise) of the company’s assets (including any distribution
-- src:9112 | of assets to members on a winding up) may be made, to the company
-- src:9113 | in respect of the treasury shares.
@ref s 76J(4) (src:9098-9113)
GIVEN `the shares are held by the company as treasury shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the payment is a dividend or another distribution (in cash or otherwise) of the company's assets, including a distribution of assets to members on a winding up` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the payment is made to the company in respect of the treasury shares` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76J(4) the dividend or distribution to the company in respect of the treasury shares is barred` MEANS
    IF    `the shares are held by the company as treasury shares`
      AND `the payment is a dividend or another distribution (in cash or otherwise) of the company's assets, including a distribution of assets to members on a winding up`
      AND `the payment is made to the company in respect of the treasury shares`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "No dividend may be paid, and no other distribution ... may be made, to the company in respect of the treasury shares"; a payment to another person, or in respect of other shares, is outside it {F-J1} {MR-b}

-- src:9115 | (5) Nothing in this section is to be taken as preventing —
-- src:9117 | (a) an allotment of shares as fully paid bonus shares in respect
-- src:9118 | of the treasury shares; or
-- src:9120 | (b) the subdivision or consolidation of any treasury share into
-- src:9121 | treasury shares of a greater or smaller number, if the total
-- src:9126 | value of the treasury shares after the subdivision or
-- src:9127 | consolidation is the same as the total value of the
-- src:9128 | treasury share before the subdivision or consolidation, as
-- src:9129 | the case may be.
@ref s 76J(5) (src:9115-9129)
GIVEN `the shares are held by the company as treasury shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `shares are allotted as fully paid bonus shares in respect of the treasury shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a treasury share is subdivided or consolidated into treasury shares of a greater or smaller number` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the total value of the treasury shares after the subdivision or consolidation is the same as the total value of the treasury share before it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76J(5) section 76J prevents the allotment, the subdivision or the consolidation` MEANS
    IF NOT `the shares are held by the company as treasury shares`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This section applies to shares which are held by a company as treasury shares"; other shares are outside it {MR-b}
    ELSE (IF    `shares are allotted as fully paid bonus shares in respect of the treasury shares`
             OR (`a treasury share is subdivided or consolidated into treasury shares of a greater or smaller number` AND `the total value of the treasury shares after the subdivision or consolidation is the same as the total value of the treasury share before it`)
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in this section is to be taken as preventing — (a) an allotment of shares as fully paid bonus shares in respect of the treasury shares; or (b) the subdivision or consolidation of any treasury share into treasury shares of a greater or smaller number, if the total value ... is the same" (a flat negative) {MR-a}
          ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection names two things the section does not prevent and says nothing of any other act {F-J2}

-- src:9133 | (6) Any shares allotted as fully paid bonus shares in respect of the
-- src:9134 | treasury shares are to be treated for the purposes of this Act as if they
-- src:9135 | were purchased by the company at the time they were allotted, in
-- src:9136 | circumstances in which section 76H applied.
@ref s 76J(6) (src:9133-9136)
GIVEN `the shares are allotted as fully paid bonus shares in respect of the treasury shares` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76J(6) the bonus shares are treated as purchased by the company at the time they were allotted, in circumstances in which section 76H applied` MEANS
    IF `the shares are allotted as fully paid bonus shares in respect of the treasury shares`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any shares allotted as fully paid bonus shares in respect of the treasury shares are to be treated"; other shares are outside it {MR-b}

DECLARE `s 76J act` IS ONE OF
    `s 76J(2) exercise a right in respect of the treasury shares`

-- src:9098 | 76J.—(1) This section applies to shares which are held by a
-- src:9099 | company as treasury shares.
-- src:9101 | (2) The company must not exercise any right in respect of the
-- src:9102 | treasury shares and any purported exercise of such a right is void.
@ref s 76J(2) (src:9098-9102)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 76J act`
`s 76J(2) the company must not exercise any right in respect of the treasury shares` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    SHANT `s 76J(2) exercise a right in respect of the treasury shares`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the company exercised a right in respect of treasury shares"

§ `Section 76K: treasury shares, disposal and cancellation`

DECLARE `s 76K(1) kind of dealing` IS ONE OF
    `s 76K(1)(a) sell the shares for cash`
    `s 76K(1)(b) transfer the shares for the purposes of or pursuant to a share scheme, whether for employees, directors or other persons`
    `s 76K(1)(c) transfer the shares as consideration for the acquisition of shares in or assets of another company or assets of a person`
    `s 76K(1)(d) cancel the shares`
    `s 76K(1)(e) sell, transfer or otherwise use the shares for another purpose the Minister has prescribed by order`
    `s 76K(1) some other dealing`

-- (1): private company. "Subject to subsection (1A)".
-- src:9140 | 76K.—(1) Subject to subsection (1A), where shares are held by a
-- src:9141 | private company as treasury shares, the company may at any time —
-- src:9143 | (a) sell the shares (or any of them) for cash;
-- src:9145 | (b) transfer the shares (or any of them) for the purposes of or
-- src:9146 | pursuant to any share scheme, whether for employees,
-- src:9147 | directors or other persons;
-- src:9149 | (c) transfer the shares (or any of them) as consideration for the
-- src:9150 | acquisition of shares in or assets of another company or
-- src:9151 | assets of a person;
-- src:9153 | (d) cancel the shares (or any of them); or
-- src:9155 | (e) sell, transfer or otherwise use the treasury shares for such
-- src:9156 | other purposes as the Minister may by order prescribe.
@ref s 76K(1) (src:9140-9156)
GIVEN `the company is a private company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the shares are held by the company as treasury shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      dealing IS A `s 76K(1) kind of dealing`
      `the Minister has by order prescribed the purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76K(1) the private company may deal with the treasury shares in this way` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the company is a private company`) OR (NOT `the shares are held by the company as treasury shares`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "where shares are held by a private company as treasury shares, the company may at any time"; any other company or share is outside it {F-K6} {MR-b}
    ELSE CONSIDER dealing
         WHEN `s 76K(1)(a) sell the shares for cash` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 76K(1)(b) transfer the shares for the purposes of or pursuant to a share scheme, whether for employees, directors or other persons` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 76K(1)(c) transfer the shares as consideration for the acquisition of shares in or assets of another company or assets of a person` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 76K(1)(d) cancel the shares` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 76K(1)(e) sell, transfer or otherwise use the shares for another purpose the Minister has prescribed by order` THEN (IF `the Minister has by order prescribed the purpose` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "for such other purposes as the Minister may by order prescribe"; the order is not among the sources
         OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "the company may at any time — (a) ...; (e) ..." lists five dealings with no "only" {F-K1} {MR-b}

-- src:9160 | (1A) A private company may cancel or dispose of treasury shares
-- src:9161 | pursuant to subsection (1) by lodging a prescribed notice of the
-- src:9162 | cancellation or disposal of treasury shares with the Registrar together
-- src:9163 | with the prescribed fee.
@ref s 76K(1A) (src:9160-9163)
GIVEN `the company is a private company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has lodged a prescribed notice of the cancellation or disposal of treasury shares with the Registrar together with the prescribed fee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76K(1A) the private company has cancelled or disposed of the treasury shares by lodging the notice` MEANS
    IF `the company is a private company` AND `the company has lodged a prescribed notice of the cancellation or disposal of treasury shares with the Registrar together with the prescribed fee`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A private company may cancel or dispose of treasury shares pursuant to subsection (1) by lodging a prescribed notice ... together with the prescribed fee", a way of doing it with no word excluding any other way {F-K2} {MR-b}

-- (1B): "does not take effect until": the bar form (ruling of 2026-11-05, item (d)).
-- src:9167 | (1B) A cancellation or disposal of treasury shares by a private
-- src:9168 | company on or after 3 January 2016 does not take effect until the
-- src:9169 | electronic register of members of the company is updated by the
-- src:9170 | Registrar under section 196A(5).
@ref s 76K(1B) (src:9167-9170)
GIVEN `the company is a private company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of the cancellation or disposal` IS A DATE
      `the electronic register of members of the company has been updated by the Registrar under section 196A(5)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76K(1B) the cancellation or disposal of the treasury shares cannot yet take effect` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the company is a private company`) OR `the date of the cancellation or disposal` LESS THAN `the day 3 January 2016`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A cancellation or disposal of treasury shares by a private company on or after 3 January 2016"; any other is outside it {F-K3} {MR-b}
    ELSE (IF `the electronic register of members of the company has been updated by the Registrar under section 196A(5)`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "does not take effect until the electronic register of members of the company is updated by the Registrar under section 196A(5)" -- once it is updated the bar is gone (ruling of 2026-11-05, item (d)) {F-K3} {MR-a}
          ELSE JUST TRUE)

-- (1C): public company; the same list as (1).
-- src:9174 | (1C) Where shares are held by a public company as treasury shares,
-- src:9175 | the company may at any time —
-- src:9180 | (a) sell the shares (or any of them) for cash;
-- src:9182 | (b) transfer the shares (or any of them) for the purposes of or
-- src:9183 | pursuant to any share scheme, whether for its employees,
-- src:9184 | directors or other persons;
-- src:9186 | (c) transfer the shares (or any of them) as consideration for the
-- src:9187 | acquisition of shares in or assets of another company or
-- src:9188 | assets of a person;
-- src:9190 | (d) cancel the shares (or any of them); or
-- src:9192 | (e) sell, transfer or otherwise use the treasury shares for such
-- src:9193 | other purposes as the Minister may by order prescribe.
@ref s 76K(1C) (src:9174-9193)
GIVEN `the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the shares are held by the company as treasury shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      dealing IS A `s 76K(1) kind of dealing`
      `the Minister has by order prescribed the purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76K(1C) the public company may deal with the treasury shares in this way` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the company is a public company`) OR (NOT `the shares are held by the company as treasury shares`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where shares are held by a public company as treasury shares, the company may at any time"; any other company or share is outside it {F-K6} {MR-b}
    ELSE CONSIDER dealing
         WHEN `s 76K(1)(a) sell the shares for cash` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 76K(1)(b) transfer the shares for the purposes of or pursuant to a share scheme, whether for employees, directors or other persons` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 76K(1)(c) transfer the shares as consideration for the acquisition of shares in or assets of another company or assets of a person` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 76K(1)(d) cancel the shares` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 76K(1)(e) sell, transfer or otherwise use the shares for another purpose the Minister has prescribed by order` THEN (IF `the Minister has by order prescribed the purpose` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "for such other purposes as the Minister may by order prescribe"; the order is not among the sources
         OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "the company may at any time — (a) ...; (e) ..." lists five dealings with no "only" {F-K1} {MR-b}

-- (1D): the public company's directors lodge within 30 days after the cancellation or disposal.
-- src:9197 | (1D) Where a public company cancels or disposes treasury shares
-- src:9198 | in accordance with subsection (1C), the directors of the company
-- src:9199 | must lodge with the Registrar a prescribed notice of the cancellation
-- src:9200 | or disposal of treasury shares together with the prescribed fee within
-- src:9201 | 30 days after the cancellation or disposal of treasury shares.
@ref s 76K(1D) (src:9197-9201)
GIVEN `the day of the cancellation or disposal of treasury shares` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 76K(1D) the last day for the directors to lodge the prescribed notice` MEANS
    `period: the last day of a period after` `the day of the cancellation or disposal of treasury shares` 30 Days

-- src:9197 | (1D) Where a public company cancels or disposes treasury shares
-- src:9198 | in accordance with subsection (1C), the directors of the company
-- src:9199 | must lodge with the Registrar a prescribed notice of the cancellation
-- src:9200 | or disposal of treasury shares together with the prescribed fee within
-- src:9201 | 30 days after the cancellation or disposal of treasury shares.
@ref s 76K(1D) (src:9197-9201)
GIVEN `the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the cancellation or disposal of treasury shares` IS A DATE
      `the directors have lodged the prescribed notice together with the prescribed fee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the prescribed notice was lodged` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76K(1D) the directors have lodged the prescribed notice in time` MEANS
    IF NOT `the company is a public company`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where a public company cancels or disposes treasury shares in accordance with subsection (1C), the directors of the company must lodge"; a private company is outside it (its own rule is (1A)) {MR-b}
    ELSE (IF    `the directors have lodged the prescribed notice together with the prescribed fee`
             AND `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` `the day of the cancellation or disposal of treasury shares` `the day the prescribed notice was lodged` 30 Days
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the directors of the company must lodge with the Registrar a prescribed notice of the cancellation or disposal of treasury shares together with the prescribed fee within 30 days after the cancellation or disposal of treasury shares" (a duty not met, the provision's own question) {F-K4} {MR-a}

DECLARE `s 76K act` IS ONE OF
    `s 76K(1D) lodge with the Registrar a prescribed notice of the cancellation or disposal of treasury shares together with the prescribed fee`
    `s 76K(3) sell or transfer the shares to which the section 215 notice relates to a person other than the person who desires to acquire them`

-- src:9197 | (1D) Where a public company cancels or disposes treasury shares
-- src:9198 | in accordance with subsection (1C), the directors of the company
-- src:9199 | must lodge with the Registrar a prescribed notice of the cancellation
-- src:9200 | or disposal of treasury shares together with the prescribed fee within
-- src:9201 | 30 days after the cancellation or disposal of treasury shares.
@ref s 76K(1D) (src:9197-9201)
GIVEN `the name of the director` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 76K act`
`s 76K(1D) the directors of the public company must lodge the prescribed notice within 30 days after the cancellation or disposal` MEANS
    PARTY Director `the name of the director`
    MUST `s 76K(1D) lodge with the Registrar a prescribed notice of the cancellation or disposal of treasury shares together with the prescribed fee`
    WITHIN 30
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Director `the name of the director` BECAUSE "the directors did not lodge the prescribed notice of the cancellation or disposal of treasury shares within 30 days"

-- (2): "cash", in relation to a sale of shares by a company, means (a) to (d). "not more than 90 days after the date on which the company agrees to sell" is counted with the keel's "not later than the end of".
-- src:9205 | (2) In subsections (1)(a) and (1C)(a), “cash”, in relation to a sale of
-- src:9206 | shares by a company, means —
-- src:9208 | (a) cash (including foreign currency) received by the
-- src:9209 | company;
-- src:9211 | (b) a cheque received by the company in good faith which the
-- src:9212 | directors have no reason for suspecting will not be paid;
-- src:9214 | (c) a release of a liability of the company for a liquidated sum;
-- src:9215 | or
-- src:9217 | (d) an undertaking to pay cash to the company on or before a
-- src:9218 | date not more than 90 days after the date on which the
-- src:9219 | company agrees to sell the shares.
@ref s 76K(2) (src:9205-9219)
GIVEN `the consideration is cash (including foreign currency) received by the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the consideration is a cheque received by the company in good faith which the directors have no reason for suspecting will not be paid` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the consideration is a release of a liability of the company for a liquidated sum` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the consideration is an undertaking to pay cash to the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date on which the company agrees to sell the shares` IS A DATE
      `the date on or before which the cash is to be paid` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76K(2) the consideration is cash` MEANS
    IF    `the consideration is cash (including foreign currency) received by the company`
       OR `the consideration is a cheque received by the company in good faith which the directors have no reason for suspecting will not be paid`
       OR `the consideration is a release of a liability of the company for a liquidated sum`
       OR (   `the consideration is an undertaking to pay cash to the company`
          AND `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` `the date on which the company agrees to sell the shares` `the date on or before which the cash is to be paid` 90 Days)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“cash”, in relation to a sale of shares by a company, means — (a) ...; (b) ...; (c) ...; or (d) ..." (a "means" definition)

-- (3): after a section 215 notice that a person desires to acquire the shares, the company must not sell or transfer the shares to which it relates except to that person.
-- src:9223 | (3) But if the company receives a notice under section 215 (Power
-- src:9224 | to acquire shares of shareholders dissenting from scheme or contract
-- src:9225 | approved by 90% majority) that a person desires to acquire any of the
-- src:9226 | shares, the company must not, under subsection (1) or (1C) (as the
-- src:9231 | case may be), sell or transfer the shares to which the notice relates
-- src:9232 | except to that person.
@ref s 76K(3) (src:9223-9232)
GIVEN `the company has received a notice under section 215 that a person desires to acquire any of the shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the shares sold or transferred are shares to which the notice relates` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the sale or transfer is to the person who desires to acquire them` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76K(3) the company is barred from selling or transferring the shares to the transferee` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the company has received a notice under section 215 that a person desires to acquire any of the shares` AND `the shares sold or transferred are shares to which the notice relates`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the company receives a notice under section 215 ... the company must not ... sell or transfer the shares to which the notice relates except to that person"; with no notice, or for shares the notice does not relate to, the subsection is silent {F-K5} {MR-b}
    ELSE (IF `the sale or transfer is to the person who desires to acquire them`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must not ... sell or transfer the shares to which the notice relates except to that person" -- the "except" is met (an "except" once met, decided site by site) {F-K5} {MR-a}
          ELSE JUST TRUE)

-- src:9223 | (3) But if the company receives a notice under section 215 (Power
-- src:9224 | to acquire shares of shareholders dissenting from scheme or contract
-- src:9225 | approved by 90% majority) that a person desires to acquire any of the
-- src:9226 | shares, the company must not, under subsection (1) or (1C) (as the
-- src:9231 | case may be), sell or transfer the shares to which the notice relates
-- src:9232 | except to that person.
@ref s 76K(3) (src:9223-9232)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
      `the company has received a notice under section 215 that a person desires to acquire any of the shares` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 76K act`
`s 76K(3) the company must not sell or transfer the shares to which the section 215 notice relates except to the person who desires to acquire them` MEANS
    IF `the company has received a notice under section 215 that a person desires to acquire any of the shares`
    THEN PARTY Company `the name of the company`
         SHANT `s 76K(3) sell or transfer the shares to which the section 215 notice relates to a person other than the person who desires to acquire them`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the company sold or transferred shares to which a section 215 notice relates to a person other than the person who desires to acquire them"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- src:9236 | (4) The directors may take such steps as are requisite to enable the
-- src:9237 | company to cancel its shares under subsection (1) or (1C) (as the case
-- src:9238 | may be) without complying with section 78B (Reduction of share
-- src:9239 | capital by private company), 78C (Reduction of share capital by
-- src:9240 | public company) or 78I (Court order approving reduction).
@ref s 76K(4) (src:9236-9240)
GIVEN `the directors take steps requisite to enable the company to cancel its treasury shares under subsection (1) or (1C)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76K(4) the directors may take the steps requisite to enable the company to cancel its shares without complying with section 78B, 78C or 78I` MEANS
    IF `the directors take steps requisite to enable the company to cancel its treasury shares under subsection (1) or (1C)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The directors may take such steps as are requisite to enable the company to cancel its shares under subsection (1) or (1C) ... without complying with section 78B ..., 78C ... or 78I"; other steps are outside it {MR-b}
